    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d206">

                <pb facs="0175" n="169" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg169"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.115/594: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-03-27T17:00:00-05:00">March 27, 1939—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>74. Reference Tientsin’s 44, March 25, 11 a.m.<anchor n="52" xml:id="d206-f1"/>
                    Peiping’s 148, March 24, 4 p.m., transmitting your 143, March 23, 9 p.m., and
                    previous telegrams in regard to the search of foreigners at Tientsin.</p>
                <pb facs="0176" n="170" xml:id="pg170"/>
                <p>Although this Government does not admit the right of Japanese authorities acting
                    directly or indirectly to search American nationals residing in China, the
                    Department is of the opinion that the situation at Tientsin does not, in view of
                    the information contained in Tientsin’s telegram no. 44, warrant the making of
                    representations at Tokyo. However, the Department desires that the Consulate
                    General at Tientsin watch the situation carefully and report developments
                    promptly in order that appropriate action may be taken should the circumstances
                    warrant.</p>
                <p>The Department has replied to an <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> of
                    March 23, 1939, from the British Embassy<anchor n="53" xml:id="d206-f2"/> in
                    regard to the matter under reference along the lines of the foregoing
                    paragraph.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Chungking and Tientsin.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
